---
import config from '../../site-config.json';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const { meta, colors, typography, header, footer, finalCta } = config;

const pageTitle = 'Terms & Conditions | ILM Assignment Help';
const pageDescription = 'The terms and conditions governing every order placed with ILM Assignment Help.';
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  faviconPath={meta.faviconPath}
  googleFontsUrl={meta.googleFontsUrl}
  fontFamily={typography.fontFamily}
  colors={colors}
>
  <Header logoText={header.logoText} logoHref="/" navLinks={header.navLinks} />

  <PageHero
    badge="Legal"
    crumbLabel="Terms & Conditions"
    h1="Terms & Conditions"
    intro="The terms that apply to every order placed with ILM Assignment Help, across WhatsApp, email, or our order platform."
  />

  <main class="page-content">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <span class="last-updated">Last updated: July 2026</span>

        <h2>1. Agreement to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By placing an order with ILM Assignment Help, whether via WhatsApp, email, or our order platform, you agree
          to these terms. They apply regardless of which channel you use to place your order.
        </p>

        <h2>2. The Service</h2>
        <p>
          We provide academic writing and assignment support for candidates studying City & Guilds ILM leadership and
          management qualifications. Our output is expert-written reference and guidance material, intended to
          support your own understanding and evidencing of your management practice. We do not guarantee a specific
          grade or assessment outcome, since that depends on factors outside our control, including your own use of
          the material and your assessor's judgement.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Orders and Payment</h2>
        <p>
          An order is confirmed once you have agreed the scope, deadline, and price with us. Pricing is based on ILM
          level, unit complexity, word count, and deadline. Payment is processed through secure third-party payment
          providers; we do not store your full card details.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Delivery</h2>
        <p>
          Completed work is delivered by email or through our order platform within the agreed timeframe. If a delay
          becomes unavoidable on our side, we will give you at least 48 hours' notice ahead of the original deadline
          where possible.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Revisions</h2>
        <p>
          Revisions are unlimited and free of charge within 14 days of delivery, provided the request is based on the
          original brief and assessment criteria. Requests that go beyond the original scope, or that are made after
          the 14-day window without an active revision already in progress, may be treated as a new order. Full
          detail is set out in our <a href="/refund-policy/">refund policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          Once an order is paid in full, the completed work is yours to use as reference and guidance material for
          your own assignment. Work that has not been paid for in full remains our property. We do not resell or
          reuse your completed order for any other client.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>
          Our output is intended as reference and guidance material to support your own academic work. You are
          responsible for using it in a way that complies with your training provider's academic integrity policy.
          See our <a href="/ilm-academic-integrity-policy/">ILM academic integrity policy</a> for the specific
          boundary between legitimate support and malpractice. Redistribution of completed work to third parties
          outside your own use is not permitted.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>
          Your personal details, employer, training provider, and order content are not shared outside the writer and
          reviewer assigned to your order. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for full detail.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Our liability for any claim relating to an order is limited to the amount paid for that order. We are not
          liable for indirect or consequential losses, including any impact on your academic outcome. This does not
          exclude or limit liability for fraud or for anything else which cannot lawfully be excluded or limited
          under the law of England and Wales.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Refund eligibility is set out in our <a href="/refund-policy/">refund policy</a> and
          <a href="/money-back-guarantee/">money-back guarantee</a>, both of which form part of these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and any dispute is subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales.</p>

        <h2>12. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always available at this page, and
          continued use of our service after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <FinalCTA heading={finalCta.heading} subtext={finalCta.subtext} button={finalCta.button} />
  <Footer
    logoText={footer.logoText}
    description={footer.description}
    columns={footer.columns}
    copyright={footer.copyright}
    contactEmail={footer.contactEmail}
    whatsapp={footer.whatsapp}
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content .container { max-width: 820px; }
</style>
